-# Masthead band. Anonymous visitors get the pitch and a single honest CTA;
-# signed-in regulars get a launch bar, because they already know what this is
-# and came here to book.
-#
-# The text column is capped at the measure rather than at a fraction of the
-# grid, so the band has no dead middle: 34rem is the 62ch paragraph plus its
-# own slack, and the readout takes the rest.
%section{class: "pt-8 pb-9 border-b border-line v2-bleed bg-hero"}
  %div{class: "grid gap-x-10 gap-y-8 items-start md:grid-cols-[minmax(0,1fr)_minmax(20rem,24rem)]"}
    %div
      - if current_user
        %h1{class: "font-display text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink"}
          Book a server
        %p{class: "text-muted mt-1"}
          Same settings as last time, or pick your own.

        -# 1-click is the fast path for someone who has booked before, so it takes
        -# the accent. "Get server" stays available for picking a time and place.
        %div{class: "flex flex-wrap gap-2 mt-5"}
          = link_to "1-click server", i_am_feeling_lucky_reservations_path, data: { turbo_method: :post, disable_with: "Finding a server…" }, class: "v2-btn v2-btn-primary", title: "Repeat your last reservation in one click"
          = link_to "Get server", new_reservation_path, class: "v2-btn v2-btn-outline", title: "Pick a time, a location and your settings"
          - if current_user.can_use_cloud_servers?
            = link_to "Cloud server", (current_user.cloud_server_access? ? new_cloud_reservation_path : cloud_info_path), class: "v2-btn v2-btn-outline", title: "Launch an on-demand cloud server"
      - else
        %h1{class: "font-display text-xl font-bold tracking-tight text-ink"}
          Your TF2 server, ready in 60 seconds.
        %p{class: "text-muted mt-3 max-w-[68ch]"}
          Free competitive TF2 servers, run by the community and paid for by donations.
          Reserve one for a scrim, a mix or an official, and get a connect string you can paste straight into Discord.

        -# One CTA, and it says where it actually goes. The previous pair sent
        -# anonymous visitors into Steam OAuth with no warning, and offered
        -# 1-click (which repeats your last reservation) to people who have none.
        %div{class: "flex flex-wrap gap-2 mt-5"}
          = link_to "/users/auth/steam", method: :post, class: "v2-btn v2-btn-primary", title: "Sign in to reserve a server" do
            Sign in through Steam

        -# Existing announcement line, kept where it has always been.
        %p{class: "text-faint mt-4"}
          New:
          = link_to "add our bot to your Discord server", discord_invite_path
    = render 'pages/v2_availability'
